  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 2003, before the US invaded Iraq, a CIA official told President George W. Bush in the Oval Office exactly where the militant leader Abu Musab al-Zarqawi was: \"He's in this camp in northeast Iraq.\" Rolf Mowatt-Larssen, a former CIA official billed on the show as a CIA chief, tells Michels he was the one who said it, in a briefing that also involved CIA director George Tenet. If true, the US knew where Zarqawi was hiding before the war began."
